SCICHEM 3.4 in the hazbrief models image (HB-167 Part B item 8)
=================================================================

What this image holds of SCICHEM: two executables built from source (runsci, scipp), seven shared
libraries built from the same source, and one data file (sciData/landuse_scichem.dat). They were built
in this image from EPRI's repository at commit 156625eff47923d232dbe4f6d055707ea3bf6ff1
(https://github.com/epri-dev/SCICHEM, committed 2025-10-23), with eleven patches
(patches/ (held privately), each with its reason in docs/evidence/hb165/probe/why.tsv) and the
build flags in deploy/models/scichem/build_engine.sh. The source of every byte is that commit and those
patches; the image is built locally from them and is not distributed as a binary.

The licence, as held
--------------------
EPRI's SourceForge project page "EPRI Air Dispersion Tools" (https://sourceforge.net/projects/epri-dispersion/,
held as corpus document epri-dispersion-sourceforge, sha256 99bfc48a93dbc9d6695947db21fde382f264398446fe2353e49c6bec1d2f9d7d)
states, verbatim:

    License BSD License

and

    SCICHEM has been migrated to GitHub: https://github.com/epri-dev/SCICHEM/releases

The GitHub repository at the commit above carries no licence file and no licence text at any depth
(corpus document scichem-tree; HB-65, HB-167). No BSD licence text naming a copyright holder is
published with SCICHEM, so none is reproduced here: a holder and terms would have to be invented.
The licence is as EPRI's public page states it. The page was fetched on 2026-10-29 (HB-69) and is
held under the key and hash above (HB-174, docs/evidence/hb174/what_is_held.md); no request to EPRI
is planned (Issue 4104d9fe, closed won't-fix; the licence gate passed in DN-018 ADDENDUM-00
section 4).

SCICHEM's two manuals, held for citation with their text withheld (corpus documents
scichem-technical-documentation-3-4 and scichem-users-guide-3-4), carry EPRI's own rights notice
on their first pages, verbatim in each:

    THIS REPORT CONTAINS PROPRIETARY INFORMATION THAT IS THE INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY OF EPRI

and EPRI "reserves all rights in the Program as delivered" (HB-170,
docs/evidence/hb170/citations_checked.tsv row C29; HB-174). That notice is the manuals'; the
declared licence above is the code's.

